WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:07.400
Most on this path run a Microsoft
365 GCC tenant with commercial Azure.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.814
Their scripts are often older than
the current tools: AzureAD cmdlets,

4
00:00:11.814 --> 00:00:16.075
a client secret in a scheduled task,
a host name written into the code.

5
00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:18.088
Some run GCC High.

6
00:00:18.088 --> 00:00:23.066
For what this module relies on: in GCC
High and DoD, the app is registered

7
00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:27.787
in the government cloud itself,
and Graph Explorer isn't supported.

8
00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:32.276
Microsoft's Azure Government
roadmap lists workload identities as

9
00:00:32.276 --> 00:00:37.001
generally available at FedRAMP High
and DoD impact levels four and five.

10
00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:41.538
And when a managed identity is an app's
federated credential, the audience

11
00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:46.075
value differs: the U S Gov token exchange
audience in the government cloud.

12
00:00:46.075 --> 00:00:50.906
The interim paths: rewrite retired-module
scripts on Graph PowerShell,

13
00:00:50.906 --> 00:00:54.673
use a certificate on premises
until the server is on Arc,

14
00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:58.180
and treat a GCC High move
as a configuration change.
